/* book.js — the hand-written half of the Atlas (readings/atlas/).
 *
 * scan.js (generated by scan.py) says what every page DOES: sign-in, pictures,
 * listening, translation, tables, score, My Page, dashboard. This file says what
 * every THING IS, where it sits on the spiral, who owns it, and what happened to it.
 *
 * RULE (Oct 2026): any chat that ships a change adds ONE dated line to that
 * thing's `notes` in the same zip — the same words it would have told Toby in chat,
 * with full URLs. New thing = new entry here + re-run scan.py. A page the scanner
 * finds that no entry claims shows up in the book as "Not filed yet".
 *
 *   id     short slug, used in links: /readings/atlas/?f=<id>
 *   ring   0 the start · 1 makers & engines · 2 every day & every week ·
 *          3 ELD 101 · 4 ELD 103 (things for both sit in the ring they're used most)
 *   kind   platform | maker | engine | activity | teacher
 *   course '101' | '103' | 'both'
 *   home   the link a person opens first (repo path, no /readings/)
 *   match  folders/files it owns (repo paths); the longest match wins; '' = the hub itself only
 *   files  engine or data files worth knowing about (not pages)
 *   own    owner chat key (see OWNERS)
 *   what   one or two plain sentences
 *   use    how Toby uses it in class (optional)
 *   chart  hand-written layer chart, only for things with no pages of their own
 *   notes  [date, task, text] newest first
 */
